"""Evidence-derived human tables; refuses replacing any delivered report."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;E=B/'evidence';read=lambda n:json.loads((E/n).read_text())
def write(name,text):
 p=B/name;assert not p.exists();p.write_text(text)
seven=read('seven-science-audit.json')['rows'];inputs={r['key']:r for r in read('fixed-inputs.json')};native={r['key']:r for r in read('native-candidate-comparison.json')['rows']}
lines=['# Original seven — exact inputs and independent disposition\n\n','**Three resolved liquid repairs; four endpoints remain unresolved.**\n\n','The original full-VLE control refuses all seven in native, Chromium and desktop WebKit. Candidate outcomes below are actual uninstrumented browser results; native A1 agrees. No failed update supplies a returned state. JSON and the original-bit columns are authoritative; displayed decimals are not replacement inputs.\n\n','| Ledger | Original rho kg/m³ | Original u J/kg | rho binary64 | u binary64 |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n']
for number in [146,148,151,152,162,164,165]:
 r=inputs[f'native-ledger-{number}'];x=r['input']['values'];h=r['input']['bits'];lines.append(f"| {number} | {x['rho']:.17g} | {x['u']:.17g} | `{h['rho']}` | `{h['u']}` |\n")
lines+=['\n| Ledger | Candidate pressure Pa | T K | h J/kg | Q / phase | Original scientific disposition |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n']
for r in [q for q in seven if q['engine']=='chromium']:
 key=r['key'];other=next(q for q in seven if q['engine']=='webkit' and q['key']==key)
 assert r['candidate'].get('state')==other['candidate'].get('state')
 if 'state' in r['candidate']:
  s=r['candidate']['state']['values'];n=native[key]['DU']['values'];assert all(s[k]==n[k] for k in ['p','h','T','rho','u','Q','phase'])
  lines.append(f"| {key.rsplit('-',1)[1]} | {s['p']:.17g} | {s['T']:.17g} | {s['h']:.17g} | 10000 sentinel / liquid | {r['disposition']} |\n")
 else:lines.append(f"| {key.rsplit('-',1)[1]} | — | — | — | No state; strict QT refusal | {r['disposition']} |\n")
lines+=['\nQ=10000 is the unchanged homogeneous DU sentinel. It is not an accepted physical mixture fraction. All scientifically accepted two-phase results require 0<=Q<=1. Supplemental invalid raw DP endpoint diagnostics are strictly refused in `evidence/quality-disposition.json` and are not part of this accepted set. Historical native A1 attempted Q values for 148/164/165 are 1.000000000000002 / 1.0000000000000018 / 1.0000000000000024; the B7 browser error confirms the strict validator refusal, not a newly measured returned Q. There is no returned quality after these errors.\n\n','## Three resolved liquids\n\n','| Ledger | Canonical Δp Pa | Canonical Δh J/kg | Canonical ΔT K | Fresh-EOS normalized energy residual | Native A1 Δp / Δh / ΔT |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n']
for r in [q for q in seven if q['engine']=='chromium' and q['physicalQualification']]:
 s=r['science'];d=s['canonical'];lines.append(f"| {r['key'].rsplit('-',1)[1]} | {d['p']:.12g} | {d['h']:.12g} | {d['T']:.12g} | {s['normalizedMassEnergy']['energy']:.12g} | 0 / 0 / 0 observed |\n")
lines+=['\nFresh/reused, Chromium/WebKit and normal/logging-on/logging-off states agree exactly in this sample. Cross-compiler acceptance still uses original tolerances. Both cached saturation coordinates equal the final evaluated coordinates and the caloric decision coordinates. Independent 65/90-digit saturation solves verify positive resolved caloric separation and cached energy error below 1e-8 J/kg. Maximum resolved-liquid final pressure/gibbs residuals are 1.3830140233e-7 Pa / 3.5587546035e-10 J/kg; maximum cached energy error is 1.2738973616e-9 J/kg. See `seven-science-audit.json` for all actual traces and independent roots.\n\n','## Four retained endpoint obligations\n\n','148: unresolved, historical invalid-Q refusal. 162: numerical liquid return, physical phase unresolved under the original reference resolution. 164: unresolved, historical invalid-Q refusal. 165: unresolved, historical invalid-Q refusal. The approximately 2.33e-9 J/kg separation at 162 is below the original 1e-8 J/kg resolution. Mathematical side information is retained separately from original scientific phase qualification.\n\n','No Q clipping, saturated-density substitution, forced vapor, alternate energy, relaxed solver limit or reference requirement is used. Default-path endpoint returns do not qualify the intended legacy Gate A path or resolve Gate B. The original seven 35-bar **browser adapter** refusals are a separate set, documented in `c1-*-explicit-bar.json` and `support-attribution.json`.\n']
write('FAILURE_MATRIX.md',''.join(lines))
perf=read('performance-summary.json');lines=['# Actual rebuilt-WASM performance and memory\n\n','These are bounded desktop browser observations, not native forecasts, kernel-only costs, sustained production throughput or physical Safari/iPad results. Five short interleaved control/candidate rounds per workload/path use at least 60 ms each. No compiler or property campaign runs concurrently with the timing campaign. Warm-up, JIT tiering, timer granularity and host variability remain relevant. Raw sample ranges, calls/second and per-request return/refusal counts are preserved in `performance-*.json`; no speedup claim is based on an individual run.\n\n','Control and candidate use the same reviewed B6 lifecycle handling. They differ scientifically only by the exact Gate A patch. All qualification identities are explicit and hash-verified.\n\n','| Engine | Path | Workload | Control median µs/call | Candidate median µs/call | Outcome comparison |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|\n']
for r in perf['rows']:
 lines.append(f"| {r['engine']} | {'full VLE' if r['fullVLE'] else 'default'} | {r['group']} | {r['control']['medianUS']:.2f} | {r['candidate']['medianUS']:.2f} | {'Matched raw outcomes' if r['comparableOutcomes'] else 'Different outcomes; ratio excluded'} |\n")
lines+=['\nLegacy resolved-liquid control calls fail while candidate calls return qualified liquid. Unresolved groups also change raw outcome mix because 162 returns. Those comparisons have **no speedup ratio**. Raw returned counts in the timing files do not certify physical phase, particularly for unresolved endpoints. Supported PH/PT/DU, genuine mixtures, repeated fresh/reused states and legitimate rejected PT are separately measured. Fresh timing includes allocation/disposal and the harness phase inspection; it is not pure EOS kernel cost. Apparent differences on unchanged paths, including variable WebKit rejected-PT timings, are descriptive short-run samples rather than evidence of an intrinsic algorithmic improvement.\n\n','## Initialization, workers and responsiveness\n\n','| Observation | Chromium | Desktop WebKit |\n|---|---:|---:|\n']
c,w=perf['engines']['chromium'],perf['engines']['webkit']
for label,key,field in [('Control median initialization ms','rebuiltB4C','medianTotalMS'),('Candidate median initialization ms','gateA','medianTotalMS'),('Candidate median first factory ms','gateA','medianFirstFactoryMS')]:
 lines.append(f"| {label} | {c['initialization'][key][field]:.2f} | {w['initialization'][key][field]:.2f} |\n")
for label,key in [('Maximum main-thread campaign heartbeat gap ms','maximumMainThreadCampaignHeartbeatGapMS'),('Maximum worker campaign heartbeat gap ms','maximumWorkerCampaignHeartbeatGapMS')]:lines.append(f"| {label} | {c[key]:.2f} | {w[key]:.2f} |\n")
for label,id in [('Control worker workload latency ms','rebuiltB4C'),('Candidate worker workload latency ms','gateA')]:lines.append(f"| {label} | {c['workerLatencyMS'][id]:.2f} | {w['workerLatencyMS'][id]:.2f} |\n")
lines+=['\nInitialization has five samples per artifact and includes explicit JS/WASM integrity checks in the research loader. Worker latency has one bounded workload sample per artifact; it includes historical sequences, errors, allocation, synthetic controls and seven full-VLE cases. Their changed error/success mix precludes a speedup ratio. Worker main-thread heartbeats are independent from worker elapsed time.\n\n','**Responsiveness concern:** observed main-thread gaps of about 1.51/1.78 seconds occur in a campaign including synchronous factory work and synchronous sampling windows. Worker campaigns still record about 77/94 ms maximum gaps. This evidence does not establish smooth interaction or device responsiveness. Numerical correctness is a separate result.\n\n','## Memory and limits\n\n','All artifacts retain original unshared memory limits: initial 344 pages / 22,544,384 bytes; maximum 32,768 pages / 2 GiB; growth enabled. Actual first factory grows memory to **56,360,960 bytes**, which remains the observed size across main/worker and repeated property workloads. Stable linear-memory size is not a leak proof.\n\n','Chromium exposes only the coarse heap observation (10,600,000 bytes throughout sampled property rounds here); it does not account for all native/WASM allocation or prove an isolated per-module heap increment. WebKit exposes no equivalent API in this run. No forced-GC or long-duration leak claim is made. All created state objects are explicitly disposed; source-level catch ownership and actual lifecycle tests provide separate evidence.\n\n','No native-performance ratio is multiplied into browser/model cost. The bounded A2 timings remain in their actual scenario evidence and are not presented as a robust simulator speed comparison. Broader performance acceptance and physical-device measurements require separate work.\n']
write('PERFORMANCE_AND_MEMORY.md',''.join(lines))
print('Failure matrix and performance/memory reports generated from retained evidence')
